From 5bf5f80e7674cefd668e2f55614c65588cea7dd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naushir Patuck <naush@raspberrypi.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Feb 2026 11:28:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: Don't overwrite request controls

Instead of overwriting the Request::controls() list, merge it with
the local list as per the 0.7 libcamera API changes.

Since libcamera v0.7.0, Camera::queueRequest() rejects a request whose
controls().infoMap() is not the camera's own ControlInfoMap. A Request
is created with such a list, but the assignment
"request->controls() = std::move(controls_)" replaces it with the
rpicam-apps ControlList, which is built from the global ControlIdMap and
has no info map. queueRequest() then logs "Overwriting Request::controls()
is not allowed", fails with -EINVAL and rpicam-apps aborts with "failed to
queue request" on the first frame. The Raspberry Pi libcamera fork does
not make this check, which is why rpicam-apps v1.7.0 still assigns.

Merge the pending controls into the request's own list instead. The
request list is empty at this point (Request::reuse() clears it), and
OverwriteExisting keeps the old semantics where the pending controls win.
controls_ is cleared afterwards, as the moved-from list used to be, so
that the controls are applied to one request only. The locking around
control_mutex_ is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Naushir Patuck <naush@raspberrypi.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/raspberrypi/rpicam-apps/commit/5bf5f80e7674cefd668e2f55614c65588cea7dd9
---
 core/rpicam_app.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/rpicam_app.cpp b/core/rpicam_app.cpp
index 9f0f80f..c187dcb 100644
--- a/core/rpicam_app.cpp
+++ b/core/rpicam_app.cpp
@@ -895,7 +895,8 @@ void RPiCamApp::queueRequest(CompletedRequest *completed_request)
 
 	{
 		std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(control_mutex_);
-		request->controls() = std::move(controls_);
+		request->controls().merge(controls_, ControlList::MergePolicy::OverwriteExisting);
+		controls_.clear();
 	}
 
 	if (camera_->queueRequest(request) < 0)
